terrible consequences of 'role-play how I say or I'll give you a nasty look'. What was wrong with the other consequences of PC actions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T05:02:56-07:00","id":1495734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1495481-disappointing-derangements?p=1495672#post1495672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm waiting for the 3rd edition; that will be awesome! Should be out sometime by the end of this decade; I can't wait!<br /> <br /> Actually, I like derangements; it provides the possibility of consequences for a player's action.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You might have to wait a long while for that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T05:10:05-07:00","id":1495735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1495481-disappointing-derangements?p=1495723#post1495723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, yes, the terrible consequences of 'role-play how I say or I'll give you a nasty look'. What was wrong with the other consequences of PC actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a werewolf and vampire storyteller, sometimes players need a little reminder that they have just butchered their mother/father/girlfriend whatever during their last frenzy or rage, I mean I wouldn't hammer them over the head with it but character derangement is a thing and it can break immersion, thankfully conditions can work the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T14:48:00-07:00","id":1495785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1495481-disappointing-derangements?p=1495672#post1495672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I like derangements; it provides the possibility of consequences for a player's action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides all the problems with how derangements were implemented, they don't really add much here Even dropping from Morality 2 to 1 is slightly favoring not gaining a derangement. The odds are that most characters aren't going to get a derangement from Morality (or equivalent) loss, because they're not going to be trying to drop their Morality into the toilet. If you have five PCs and they all manage to keep to Morality 4+, you might see one or two derangements between the group.<br /> <br /> For non-mortals, the mechanical consequences of losing their Morality equivalent was far more important than the potential of gaining a derangement.<br /> <br /> Also, there were something like 40 derangement pairs printed over the course of 1e; though this includes a number of variants that interact with things like Frenzy, as well as ones that are exclusive to specific supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Whatever your feelings about 2e are here, the Integrity system ensures there are always consequences for actions, as every result on a breaking point check has an impact of the PC. Even an Exceptional Success, which doesn't impart a Condition to resolve like all the other do, refills 1 WP and gives you an extra Beat as your character comes through the trying event more resolute and experienced. Consequences don't have to be bad after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T21:23:35-07:00","id":1495940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1495481-disappointing-derangements?p=1495785#post1495785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .<br /> <br /> Whatever your feelings about 2e are here, the Integrity system ensures there are always consequences for actions, as every result on a breaking point check has an impact of the PC. Even an Exceptional Success, which doesn't impart a Condition to resolve like all the other do, refills 1 WP and gives you an extra Beat as your character comes through the trying event more resolute and experienced. Consequences don't have to be bad after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have no feelings about 2e, other than NWoD is relatively new to me. I'm sure it has some excellent-solutions for problems in 1e, just like Requiem solved a lot of problems with the Masquerade. Good news is that I can still probably find 2e books without a used book-seller trying to sell me a poor, used-copy of a NWoD-book, for thrice the original-price because it's a, &quot;Collector's item&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T01:21:32-07:00","id":1495946,"title":"","content":"Well, for the most part, buying any CofD book 1e or 2e (I know it's a bit confusing, the old books are titled &quot;World of Darkness&quot; but there was a branding change as the 20th anniversary editions of the classic WoD books started selling a lot), you can get them via DriveThruRPG as either pdfs for Print-on-Demand. The shipping costs aren't great depending on where you live relative to where DTRPG has a printer, but if you want physical copies that's probably the most reliable way to go. You can always point out that the books just changed printers and aren't out of print since you can get fresh printed copies whenever you want if you think someone's trying to gouge you by calling one of the books a collector's item.<br /> <br /> Since you already have the 1e core book, you can get a free file from DTRPG called the &quot;God-Machine Rule Update,&quot; which is a guide to updating the 1e core rules to the 2e ones (obviously as an early thing, it's not 100% the same as the full 2e books) to get a feel of the changes to the baseline rules.<br /> <br /> It's also worth considering that three of the supernatural games (Demon, Beast, and Deviant) only run on the 2e rules, so there's another reason to consider looking into the 2e stuff before you go too deep on the older book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}